# Ordered CoE setup for velocity PDO map (kernel elc_setup batch).
# Applied in PREOP by iod (ECSETUPRECIPE / --setup-recipe) before cycle activate.
#
# Objects that must not be zero when the slave enters OP while in PP/PV should
# be written here as SDO (not only left to cyclic PDO defaults). Plant may use
# several ECSETUPRECIPE machines for different positions / values.
#
# Format: sequence position type index subindex value
# POS is expanded per target bus position by iod.
1  POS u8  0x1c12 0 0
2  POS u8  0x1c13 0 0
3  POS u8  0x1600 0 0
4  POS u8  0x1a00 0 0
5  POS u32 0x1600 1 0x60400010
6  POS u32 0x1600 2 0x60ff0020
7  POS u32 0x1600 3 0x60830020
8  POS u32 0x1600 4 0x60840020
9  POS u32 0x1600 5 0x60e00010
10 POS u32 0x1600 6 0x60e10010
11 POS u32 0x1a00 1 0x60410010
12 POS u32 0x1a00 2 0x606c0020
13 POS u32 0x1a00 3 0x60770010
14 POS u32 0x1a00 4 0x603f0010
15 POS u8  0x1600 0 6
16 POS u8  0x1a00 0 4
17 POS u16 0x1c12 1 0x1600
18 POS u16 0x1c13 1 0x1a00
19 POS u8  0x1c12 0 1
20 POS u8  0x1c13 0 1
# PREOP object values (before OP). Profile accel/decel must be non-zero if
# mode is PP/PV and these objects are RxPDO-mapped (cyclic can otherwise
# write 0 while outputs are zero-gated). Plant ANALOGOUTPUT defaults should
# match; use extra ECSETUPRECIPE entries for per-group values if needed.
21 POS u32 0x6083 0 200000
22 POS u32 0x6084 0 200000
23 POS u8  0x6060 0 3
